  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the baby as the potential agent of the vulgar action",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the baby (visual material) as the implied subject of the punchline 'shit on it.' The meme uses the baby's innocence and the visual of the baby sitting on the couch to create an incongruous scenario where the user (as the viewer) is humorously invited to imagine the baby as the one who might commit the taboo act. This projection relies on the baby's visual representation and the textual punchline to create a shared humorous experience where the user identifies with the baby as the potential 'culprit.'",
